n could definitely confirm to John  that he is not Ned's son but I think  there may be another way John can find  out who his mother is I think John can  still find out who his mother is by the  same man who promised to tell him in the  first place is my mother alive  does she know about me where I am where  I'm going  as you care the next time we see each  other we'll talk about your mother I  promise  Ned made a promise to John that the next  time they see each other he would tell  him about his mother but unfortunately  we know how this part of the story ends  John goes to the wall to become a  brother of the Nights Watch and that  goes to King's Landing where he has  eventually beheaded by the bastard false  King Joffrey this was one of the most  shocking and tragic turn of events not  only because the late great Honorable  Ned Stark was killed but also because  Jon Snow never got those answers he was  looking for and I know a lot of people  say who cares if Jon ever finds out what  purpose does it serve to the story  whether John finds this out I understand  what you're saying but wouldn't you want  to know I personally don't mind spending  a few minutes of Showtime for Jon to  learn of this even though we're running  out of time with only 13 episodes left  it wouldn't bother me to dedicate  several scenes to this I think Jon  deserves to know but you're probably  wondering how the hell Ned Stark can  keep this promise now that he's dead he  promised Jon that the next time they see  each other he would tell him about his  mother well how the hell is he going to  do this now let's first think about the  promise Ned fulfill to Liana she asked  Ned to promise to keep John safe because  if Robert ever found out he would kill  her baby and we definitely know Robert  is willing to do something like this  he wanted Daenerys and her baby killed  so I do think he would have had John  killed too but in order for Ned to keep  this a secret he had to lie too damn  near eve